#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186649977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e21dc5f-5a5e-55da-87c8-e2f9c689c401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=41i-31j+23k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649972} {:answer/id #uuid "20f5a3c7-a0cd-5eb1-8a11-5ef6d32e799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=23i+31j-41k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649973} {:answer/id #uuid "59df5186-2517-50e6-a29d-5983ee8cd661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=31i-41j+23k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649974} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0b9c7e-802d-5d18-97cc-2fdab405a4c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=41i-31j+23k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649975} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a7241f-9bb0-58a3-a055-665ee79f6a11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=23i-41j-31k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649976} {:answer/feedback "Locally authored correction by Codex; this option was absent from the original Math Academy bank." :answer/id #uuid "2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=-41i+31j-23k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Locally authored correction by Codex; this option was absent from the original Math Academy bank." :answer/id #uuid "2889dceb-0038-550a-b032-295566f22cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=-41i+31j-23k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649978} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1439bbb-bd02-5648-b8fa-4994eaa3e108" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9705608-d638-5e5d-b560-a728314a7a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-104098" :question/problem "A line passes through the points  $P(-3,-1,4)$ and $Q(1,8,9).$ Find its vector equation in the form $r\\times v=c.$" :question/worked-solution "Local correction by Codex. The five original Math Academy choices are retained; the additional correct equation is locally authored. Math Academy's grading key for the original bank is unconfirmed.\n\nWe need a vector parallel to the line. Using the two given points,\n\n$$\nv=q-p=\\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\8\\\\9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\\\-1\\\\4\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\\\9\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nStarting with $(r-p)\\times v=0$, we obtain $r\\times v=p\\times v$. Expanding the cross product gives\n\n$$\np\\times v=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\-3&-1&4\\\\4&9&5\\end{vmatrix}\n=(-5-36)i-( -15-16)j+(-27+4)k=-41i+31j-23k.\n$$\n\nThus the equation is\n\n$$\nr\\times\\begin{bmatrix}4\\\\9\\\\5\\end{bmatrix}=-41i+31j-23k.\n$$\n\nBoth given points satisfy this equation: $P\\times v=Q\\times v=(-41,31,-23)$. None of the five original choices does.\n\nOriginal Math Academy explanation (preserved verbatim below; its concluding signs are incorrect):\n\nWe know that the line passes through the points $P(-3,-1,4)$ and $Q(1,8,9).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =q-p \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, starting with the equation of the line using the cross product, we manipulate the equation and then substitute in our values of $p$ and $v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v-p\\times v & =0 \\\\ r\\times v & =p\\times v \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ r\\times \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =-41i-31j+23k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
